      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-09-07T20:56:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Once a port leaves SRC_DISCOVERY, this flag will never be set until EC goes to suspend for other reason (and hit this line again). How do we deal with a port which becomes idle in SRC_DISCOVERY again?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3169,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 3169,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "fb46de852f5123ea1b945fcb4d00ee409e94f651",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cde9069e_fe3709d5",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 3169,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-09-07T21:02:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we\u0027re still in suspend, the port won\u0027t role toggle, so the ways out of SRC_DISCOVERY are:\n\n- Detach, in which case we\u0027ll stay a sink for as long as we\u0027re in suspend, so we\u0027ll never get back to SRC_DISCOVERY.\n\n- The port responds to our source cap, in which case it speaks PD, so we don\u0027t want to go to deep sleep (until detach, see above).",
      "parentUuid": "2471a8b2_5047b197",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3169,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 3169,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "fb46de852f5123ea1b945fcb4d00ee409e94f651",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
